{"type":"npc","name":"Vigil Flame","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":75,"temp":0,"max":75,"details":""},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"fire","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold","value":5,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"poison","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"void","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["requian"],"details":"Can't speak any language, Manifest empathy"},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Ideally, graveyards are places of memory and repose, where the physical bodies of the dead can rest while their souls migrate to the afterlife. However, soul energy often pools and gathers in these places, and this excess soul energy is at risk of forming into incorporeal undead and restless spirits if left to its own devices. To help this energy pass on, cultures that respect the gods of life and death often place lanterns in graveyards to stand a silent vigil over the souls of the dead.</p><p>When enough soul energy gathers around one of these vigil lanterns, it can manifest a new consciousness devoted to the cause of shepherding lost souls. And when these consciousnesses bond with the energy of Purgatory, they can form a nascent psychopomp called a vigil flame, one of the few psychopomps to complete the process of creation in the mortal realm instead of Purgatory. These vigil flames lend their aid to both the living and the dead, but they despise undead as the ultimate insult to the natural order. Despite their benevolent demeanor, they are true servants of the cycle of life and death, and they don't hesitate to usher hesitant lost, restless, or malevolent souls into the afterlife by force.</p><p>Of all the undead that roam the world, none inspire vigil flames to fight as fiercely as spiritflame lanterns, which represent a perversion of their form and purpose.</p><h2>Grave Lights</h2><p>While a vigil flame's first duty is to the dead, they are often found leading the living as well. They sometimes pause their eternal war with undeath to escort a hapless traveler safely through undead-haunted wastes—or to beckon competent adventurers further into those wastes, in order to team up against an undead threat that the vigil flame can't defeat alone.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Diplomacy, Medicine, Occultism, Religion)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, burning barbs, charisma, death, dexterity, energy resistant (fire, vitality, void), fire, fire shield, fortification, life, lifeward armor, light, spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.rfZpqmj0AIIdkVIs]{Heal}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.DyiD239dNS7RIxZE]{Holy Light}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.0qaqksrGGDj74HXE]{Revealing Light}), throwing, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Tullio Grasso","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":0},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":15,"senses":[{"type":"lifesense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":12,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":12},"diplomacy":{"base":13},"medicine":{"base":13},"occultism":{"base":11},"religion":{"base":13}},"traits":{"value":["fire","monitor","psychopomp"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"ti